# Runtime-generated data, not source data: fills up from real usage on each
# teammate's machine (the live decision ledger, the point-in-time archive) --
# committing it would create constant merge conflicts and grow the repo with
# data that's either empty on a fresh clone or regeneratable
# (data_builders.pit_archive.archive_all_sources()), not something teammates
# need to share via git. raw_data/ itself (the real harvested source data
# the whole system depends on) is intentionally NOT ignored -- that's real,
# hard-won input data, not a build artifact.
raw_data/ledger/
raw_data/pit_archive/
# opt.weather_window's disk cache for live Open-Meteo marine forecasts --
# 12-hour TTL, re-fetched constantly, keyed by rounded lat/lon and today's
# date. Regenerated on demand (falls back to None, never breaks a quote, if
# absent); not source data any teammate needs to share via git.
raw_data/open_meteo/
# The user account and session database (auth.store). Real per-deployment
# state: password hashes and live session tokens. Committing it would publish
# credential material and hand every clone the same accounts -- the accounts
# on one deployment are nobody else's business, and a fresh clone is supposed
# to start with none and bootstrap its own first admin.
raw_data/auth/

# IBTrACS is the one exception to "raw_data/ is intentionally tracked" above:
# the ALL-list CSV is hundreds of MB, too large to commit sensibly. Only
# PULL_NOTES.md (source/licence/citation) and the derived
# src/data/cyclone_climatology.parquet are committed -- see
# data_builders.harvest_ibtracs and data_builders.build_cyclone_climatology.
raw_data/ibtracs/*.csv

# Sentinel-1 SAR scenes -- real GRD products are ~1.2-2.0 GB each (measured
# live, see data_builders.harvest_sentinel1's own module docstring). Only
# PULL_NOTES.md is committed. The detection-overlay PNGs anchorage renders
# from a real scene are also large (~8 MB each, full-resolution crops) and
# regenerable from the scene, so they are ignored here too -- a small,
# presentation-ready copy of the one worth keeping lives in
# docs/screenshots/ instead, which IS committed.
raw_data/sentinel1/*.zip
raw_data/sentinel1/*.SAFE
raw_data/sentinel1/*.tiff
raw_data/sentinel1/*.png

# anchorage.render's per-(port, scene_id) overlay PNGs (served live by
# GET /anchorage/{port}/overlay.png) are NO LONGER ignored.
#
# They were, on the reasoning that they are "regenerable from the real scene +
# census, not source data" -- the same argument as the sentinel1/*.png entry
# above. That argument is sound for anyone who has the scenes, and it does not
# hold for anyone who clones this repo: regenerating an overlay needs the
# Sentinel-1 GRD scenes (6.8 GB, not in the repo) AND Copernicus credentials.
# Tested on a fresh clone, GET /anchorage/{port}/overlay.png returned 404 for
# every port, so the satellite panel -- a headline feature -- fell back to its
# text-only view with a console 404, on a machine that had done nothing wrong.
#
# All five are 4.1 MB in total, which is not a meaningful cost against being
# the difference between the feature working and not working out of the box.
# The 6.8 GB of source scenes stay ignored; only the rendered crops ship.
#
# census.jsonl is likewise NOT ignored -- that IS the real observation, kept
# the same way opt/ledger's log is.